    {
      "start_time": 80,
      "end_time": 360,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The science fiction movie "
            },
            {
              "text": "Starship Troopers",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": " directed by Paul Verhoeven is an adaptation of "
            },
            {
              "text": "Starship Troopers ",
              "italic": true
            },
            {
              "text": "by Robert A Heinlein. The movie is a satire of the militarism of America and fascism which is evidenced by the director's commentary. "
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Genres",
          "tag": "Science Fiction"
        },
        {
          "category": "Forms",
          "tag": "Movie"
        },
        {
          "category": "Science Fiction",
          "tag": "Politics"
        },
        {
          "category": "Science Fiction",
          "tag": "Futuristic"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "1e390d82-4394-46b6-b1b9-86719116fd3c"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 361,
      "end_time": 440,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The protagonist of Starship Troopers, Johny Rico, is a white man from Argentina. Casper Van Dein talks about how Johny Rico was the descendant of Nazis who fled to Argentina after the Second World War."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Genres",
          "tag": "Science Fiction"
        },
        {
          "category": "Forms",
          "tag": "Movie"
        },
        {
          "category": "Science Fiction",
          "tag": "Politics"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "cbd3bc6b-b515-4db5-a3fe-65159d5d1ae9"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 440,
      "end_time": 540,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The note of Mormon extremism is a direct reference to American history through this detail of the world-building as a direct critique of America's colonial past. "
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
          "category": "Genres",
          "tag": "Science Fiction"
        },
        {
          "category": "Forms",
          "tag": "Movie"
        },
        {
          "category": "Science Fiction",
          "tag": "Politics"
        },
        {
          "category": "Science Fiction",
          "tag": "Dystopian"
        }
      ],
      "uuid": "a1e22efa-fd49-49b9-8846-c207650ac446"
    },
    {
      "start_time": 541,
      "end_time": 600,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The shower scene satirises the policies and positions of America's past, particularly the exclusion of rights from groups of people, and the way the military recruits vulnerable people by offering to pay for their college tuition in exchange for military service. "
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        {
